    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Hurrikan',
            subtitle: 'The German Sweep Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Hurrikan (Hurricane) is a German fishing card game closely related to the Italian classic 'Scopa' and its Spanish cousin 'Escoba'. Players capture cards from a central layout by matching values from their hand. The game is named for the 'Hurrikan' move (a 'Sweep'), where a player captures all cards from the table in a single turn.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "A regional adaptation of 'Scopa' that migrated to Germany. It preserves the core capturing mechanics but uses standard or German-suited cards and a specific point-target of 16.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2 players (Standard).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Usually 32-40 cards. If using 52, remove 8s, 9s, 10s. Ranking: Ace (1), 2-7 (Face), Jack (8), Queen (9), King (10).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard deck of cards.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal 3 cards to each player and 4 face-up on the table.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Scopa: The Italian original with 40 cards.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Escoba: Spanish variant where you must sum to 15.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Cirulla: A highly complex Ligurian variant.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
    description: "Hurrikan (Hurricane) is a German fishing card game closely related to the Italian classic 'Scopa' and its Spanish cousin 'Escoba'. Players capture cards from a central layout by matching values from their hand. The game is named for the 'Hurrikan' move (a 'Sweep'), where a player captures all cards from the table in a single turn.",
    tags: [
