          equipment: 'Standard deck of cards.',
          dealing: 'Deal 3 cards to each player and 4 face-up on the table.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Score 16 points by capturing cards and completing 'Hurrikans'.",
          gameplay: '1. On your turn, play one card from your hand. 2. Capture: If your card matches a card on the table, you take both. If your card matches the SUM of multiple cards on the table, you take all of them. 3. Priority: You MUST capture a single card of equal value before combining cards. 4. The Hurrikan (Sweep): If your capture leaves the table empty, you score 1 bonus point. 5. If you cannot capture, you must add your card to the table.',
          keyRules: [
            'You MUST capture a single card of equal value before combining cards',
            'The Hurrikan (Sweep): capturing all cards from the table scores 1 bonus point',
            'Scoring: Most cards (1 pt), Most Hearts (1 pt), Seven of Hearts (1 pt), Each Hurrikan (1 pt)',
            'First to 16 points wins the match',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize capturing Heart cards and the Seven of Hearts above all else. Try to leave your opponent with no combinations that sum to 10 (the maximum face card value).',
          intermediate: "Denial: If you see the table has a 3, a 4, and an Ace (Sum = 8), and you don't have an 8, avoid playing a card that would make the total sum to a Jack, Queen, or King.",
          advanced: 'Counting 7s: The Sevens are the most powerful cards for building combinations. If you know three 7s are gone, you can safely play high cards without fearing a Hurrikan.',
          tips: [
            "Save your '10' (King) for when the board has many low cards that sum to 10.",
            "Never leave a single card on the table if you can help it, as it's an easy setup for an opponent's Hurrikan.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
